@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api

### Is the server up?
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### A route that doesn't exist (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/nothing-here

### Broken JSON in the body (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/health
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": }

### First page of recipes (24 per page, most popular first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes

### Vegetarian desserts ready in 30 minutes, quickest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes?course=Dessert&diet=vegetarian&maxTime=30&sort=quickest

### Page 2, with 5 per page
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes?page=2&limit=5

### Bad values (expect 400 with a message for each field)
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes?course=Lunch&limit=500&page=abc

### The allowed values for each filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes/filters


### Search: best matches first (+ means a space in a URL)
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes?q=paneer+butter+masala&limit=5

### Search inside one course
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes?q=dosa&course=Breakfast&limit=5

### A half-typed word: falls back to matching letters inside titles
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes?q=panee&limit=5

### One recipe, with similar dishes
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes/masala-karela

### A recipe that doesn't exist (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes/no-such-dish

### Not a valid slug (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes/Masala_Karela

### Create an account (send it twice: the second time gives 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ankur Singh",
  "email": "ankur@example.com",
  "password": "masala-dosa-42"
}

### Missing and invalid fields (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### Log in. REST Client keeps the cookie that comes back and sends it with later requests.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ankur@example.com",
  "password": "masala-dosa-42"
}

### Who am I? (needs the login cookie)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### Wrong password (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ankur@example.com",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Log out. Afterwards, "Who am I?" gives 401.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

### Log out of all devices: every login token made before this stops working
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout-all

### Try a token you copied before "log out of all devices" (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Cookie: rasoi_token=PASTE-THE-OLD-TOKEN-HERE

### Cook with what you have (+ means a space in a URL)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pantry/recipes?have=onion,tomato,potato,green+chilli,ginger,garlic,coriander+leaves&limit=6

### The same pantry, without assuming salt, oil, water and the spice box
GET {{baseUrl}}/pantry/recipes?have=onion,tomato,potato,green+chilli,ginger,garlic,coriander+leaves&staples=false&spices=false&limit=3

### Paneer night: main courses only
GET {{baseUrl}}/pantry/recipes?have=paneer,onion,tomato,capsicum,butter,cream,ginger,garlic&course=Main+Course&limit=5

### Nothing in the pantry (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pantry/recipes

### Ingredient autocomplete: "jee" finds cumin seeds through its Hindi name, jeera
GET {{baseUrl}}/ingredients?q=jee

### Autocomplete matches the start of any word: "chil" finds green chilli
GET {{baseUrl}}/ingredients?q=chil

### Your pantry in Hindi: pyaz, tamatar, aloo, hari mirch, adrak, lehsun, dhania
GET {{baseUrl}}/pantry/recipes?have=pyaz,tamatar,aloo,hari+mirch,adrak,lehsun,dhania&limit=6

### Plurals and a word Rasoi doesn't know
GET {{baseUrl}}/pantry/recipes?have=onions,tomatoes,unicorn&limit=3

### Save your pantry (log in first: the "Log in" request above)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/pantry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": ["Pyaz", "tamatar", "aloo", "jeera", "dahi", "onions", "unicorn"]
}

### Your saved pantry
GET {{baseUrl}}/pantry


### ---------- PANTRY TEST: send these from top to bottom ----------
### Empty the saved pantry (to run the test again from the start)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/pantry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": []
}
### 1. Log in
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ankur@example.com",
  "password": "masala-dosa-42"
}

### 2. Your saved pantry (empty at first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pantry

### 3. Save your pantry
PUT {{baseUrl}}/pantry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": ["Pyaz", "tamatar", "aloo", "jeera", "dahi", "onions", "unicorn"]
}

### 4. Your saved pantry again (now it has 5 items)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pantry

### 5. Log out
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout

### 6. Your saved pantry after logging out (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pantry


# ---------- SAVED RECIPES (log in first) ----------

### Save a recipe
PUT {{baseUrl}}/saved/masala-karela

### Save another
PUT {{baseUrl}}/saved/tomato-garlic-chutney

### And a third
PUT {{baseUrl}}/saved/paneer-butter-masala

### Your saved recipes, most recently saved first
GET {{baseUrl}}/saved

### Un-save one
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/saved/tomato-garlic-chutney


# ---------- REVIEWS ----------

### Write your review
PUT {{baseUrl}}/recipes/paneer-butter-masala/reviews/mine
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Restaurant-style, and easier than I expected."
}

### Change your review: the same request with a new rating
PUT {{baseUrl}}/recipes/paneer-butter-masala/reviews/mine
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 4,
  "comment": "Very good. A little too much cream for me."
}

### A second person: sign up as Priya (REST Client is now logged in as Priya)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Priya Sharma",
  "email": "priya@example.com",
  "password": "gulab-jamun-9"
}

### Priya's review
PUT {{baseUrl}}/recipes/paneer-butter-masala/reviews/mine
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 3,
  "comment": "Good gravy, but it took me longer than an hour."
}

### Everyone's reviews, newest first (no login needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes/paneer-butter-masala/reviews

### The recipe page, with "saved" and "myReview" for whoever is logged in
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes/paneer-butter-masala

### Most popular first: reviewed recipes rise to the top
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes?limit=3

### Delete your review
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/recipes/paneer-butter-masala/reviews/mine

### Not a valid rating (expect 400)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/recipes/paneer-butter-masala/reviews/mine
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 6
}


### ---------- MEAL PLANNER (log in first) ----------
# A week is named by its Monday. Paste meal ids from the responses into these two lines:
@pongalMeal = PASTE-THE-PONGAL-MEAL-ID
@riceMeal = PASTE-THE-RICE-MEAL-ID

### This week's plan (empty at first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/planner/2026-11-02

### Monday dinner: Paneer Butter Masala for 6 (the recipe serves 4)
POST {{baseUrl}}/planner/2026-11-02/meals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "day": 0,
  "slot": "dinner",
  "recipe": "paneer-butter-masala",
  "servings": 6
}

### Tuesday breakfast: Pudina Khara Pongal for 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/planner/2026-11-02/meals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "day": 1,
  "slot": "breakfast",
  "recipe": "pudina-khara-pongal",
  "servings": 2
}

### Wednesday lunch: Spicy Tomato Rice, as the recipe is written (no servings)
POST {{baseUrl}}/planner/2026-11-02/meals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "day": 2,
  "slot": "lunch",
  "recipe": "spicy-tomato-rice"
}

### Move the pongal to Thursday, and make it for 4
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/planner/2026-11-02/meals/{{pongalMeal}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "day": 3,
  "servings": 4
}

### Remove the tomato rice (send it twice: the second time gives 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/planner/2026-11-02/meals/{{riceMeal}}

### The week's grocery list
GET {{baseUrl}}/planner/2026-11-02/grocery

### A Tuesday isn't a week (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/planner/2026-11-03